(Low-Pressure Ignition of Cotton Fabric \(LPIC\)) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
0 -30 Td
15 TL
(Test report LPIC-TR-01, November 2026) '
() '
(1. Objective) '
(The objective of the LPIC experiment was to find whether thin cotton fabric) '
(ignites and keeps burning in oxygen-enriched air at reduced pressure, the kind) '
(of atmosphere planned for a Moon base. The purpose is fire prevention: to know) '
(which cabin atmospheres make common fabrics easier to ignite.) '
() '
(The experiment ran in a drop tower, giving 5.2 seconds of microgravity per test,) '
(and the same tests were repeated in normal gravity \(1 g\) for comparison.) '
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
60 40 Td
(FICTIONAL TEST REPORT - written to test the Ghostflame upload feature. Not NASA data.  Page 1) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
