stream
BT
/F2 15 Tf
60 780 Td
(3. Results) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
0 -30 Td
15 TL
(Main result: in microgravity, cotton did not keep burning at 21 % oxygen at) '
(either pressure, but it burned to the end of the sample at 30 % and 34 %) '
(oxygen at both 101.3 kPa and 56.5 kPa.) '
() '
(Flame spread rate in microgravity \(mean of two tests, mm/s\):) '
(   O2 %    101.3 kPa    56.5 kPa) '
(   21      no spread    no spread) '
(   26      0.8          no spread) '
(   30      1.9          1.4) '
(   34      2.6          2.1) '
() '
(At the same oxygen level, flame spread was about 25 % slower at 56.5 kPa than) '
(at 101.3 kPa. In normal gravity the flames spread 2 to 3 times faster than in) '
(microgravity and cotton also burned at 21 % oxygen.) '
(Conclusion: Moon-base air \(34 % O2, 56.5 kPa\) lets cotton fabric burn in) '
(microgravity, even though the pressure is lower.) '
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
60 40 Td
(FICTIONAL TEST REPORT - written to test the Ghostflame upload feature. Not NASA data.  Page 3) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
